1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,081
This is the Dermalogica Retinol Clearing Oil.

2
00:00:03,081 --> 00:00:08,059
In the next few minutes, we'll go through what it does, what's inside, and exactly

3
00:00:08,059 --> 00:00:08,908
how to use it.

4
00:00:09,669 --> 00:00:11,753
It's a face oil with two jobs.

5
00:00:11,753 --> 00:00:17,588
Retinol works on skin recovery and signs of aging, and salicylic acid targets active

6
00:00:17,588 --> 00:00:18,283
breakouts.

7
00:00:19,052 --> 00:00:23,873
The retinol is slow-release, and it works all night to help optimize skin recovery.

8
00:00:24,573 --> 00:00:29,288
It helps reduce the appearance of fine lines, wrinkles, and hyperpigmentation.

9
00:00:29,988 --> 00:00:34,660
Then there's salicylic acid, which targets active breakouts to help clear skin.

10
00:00:35,360 --> 00:00:40,105
All of this is powered by a lipid-based delivery system, which actively nourishes

11
00:00:40,105 --> 00:00:42,917
the skin with skin-mimicking phytoactive lipids.

12
00:00:43,676 --> 00:00:48,561
Those lipids come from three oils: argan, rosehip seed, and golden jojoba.

13
00:00:49,261 --> 00:00:50,564
Here's how to use it.

14
00:00:50,564 --> 00:00:52,301
This one is for the evening.

15
00:00:52,301 --> 00:00:55,341
At night, after cleansing, it goes on clean skin.

16
00:00:56,041 --> 00:00:59,083
Press the button and release it to fill the dropper.

17
00:00:59,083 --> 00:01:03,764
Then gently press the button again to dispense six to ten drops into your hands.

18
00:01:04,464 --> 00:01:08,048
Smooth the oil over your face and neck, avoiding the eye area.

19
00:01:08,748 --> 00:01:11,905
The slow-release retinol then works all night, while you sleep.

20
00:01:12,605 --> 00:01:18,057
That's the Retinol Clearing Oil: slow-release retinol, salicylic acid for active

21
00:01:18,057 --> 00:01:23,032
breakouts, argan, rosehip and jojoba oils, and six to ten drops at night.

22
00:01:23,032 --> 00:01:25,145
The link is in the description.
